WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.582
CTEs are not automatically better.

00:00:02.582 --> 00:00:05.612
A short query may be clearer without one.

00:00:05.612 --> 00:00:09.322
A CTE also does not repair unclear grain.

00:00:09.322 --> 00:00:12.837
And it does not automatically make a query faster.

00:00:12.837 --> 00:00:17.717
Use named stages when they improve reasoning and maintainability.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:24.757
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:32.857
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:32.857 --> 00:00:39.760
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
